quran[5]{c,v,t}:
  5,104,"And when it is said to them: ‘Come to what Allah has revealed and (come) to the Messenger,’ they say: ‘What we have found our forefathers practising is good enough for us.’ What! Even if their forefathers did not know anything and were not guided?"
  5,105,O believers! Take care of your own souls. The one who deviates from the right path cannot harm you if you are rightly guided. To Allah shall be your return all together. Then He shall inform you regarding what you used to do.
  5,106,"O believers! When death approaches any of you while making a will, the witness between you shall be two just persons among you; otherwise, two from among others (i.e. non-muslims, if Muslim witnesses are not available). It is (needed) if you are travelling in the land and the calamity of death befalls you. You shall detain the two of them after prayer, and if you doubt (their testimony), then they shall testify under oath (saying): ‘By Allah! We will never sell it for any price, even if he were a close relative, nor will we conceal the testimony of Allah, for then we would surely be among the sinful.’"
  5,107,"If it is found that both of them were guilty of sin (i.e. perjury), then let two others stand in their place from those most entitled as claimants (among the deceased’s closest heirs affected by the bequest). Then they should swear by Allah (saying:) ‘Our testimony is truer than their testimony, and we have not transgressed. Otherwise, we would indeed be among the wrongdoers.’"
  5,108,It is more likely that they (i.e. the witnesses) will give the testimony in its accurate form or fear that their oaths might be refuted by other oaths afterwards. Be conscious of Allah and listen. Allah does not guide the transgressing people.
